Z||000000||JamesWM83||08-14-2001||01:46 AM||||Would this help cooling off the engine any? I know that heat rises.. but there's no way it's rising out as much as possible when the deckilde is in the way... what kind of scoop shoudl I use? Or should I just toy around and make my own? Show me some examples if you can... and if I don't like the looks I'll just design my own.. I've got the time <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Thanks guys... God I love this message board. Lates<P>------------------<BR>~James<P>1986 Fiero GT! <BR>2.8 4 clicker. White face guages, blue backlighting, grey marlbe dash kit, IRM sie rocker scoops, fierostore.com 1/4 window scoop, V8 Archie Warber hood, rear added sway bar, silver mesh inserts in tail-lights, mesh inserts in turn lamp and grill, KYB shocks and struts, Eibach lowering springs, 300 watt amp, and 600 watt 12" sub, clarion pro audio 5x6" plates, Kenwood Xcelon 4x10's, clarion pro audio cd player, monster calbe wiring, rockford wiring, pheonix gold wiring, chrome ocelot exhaust tips||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-14-2001||10:05 AM||||Ok, this is nearly the same scoop I bought from outlawperformance.org a while back (They're gone now...) I haven't had a chance to install it yet.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tomscoop.jpg"> <P>Anyway, it came from Tom's Accessories at <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/tom/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/tom/</A><P>This scoop is nice because it follows the lines of the car quite well, and adds a nice vent for the engine.  You also can install small electrical fans under the vents next to the decklid- that should increase airflow as well.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
